#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: KhAN
#> pause: 45
#> must: In XANadu did Kubla Khan
#> must: In XANadu did Kubla KhAN
#> must: KhAN Kubla did In XANadu
#> not: pleasure dome
#> source: \2 \1
# 12. First match or all matches, and \1 \2 in the replacement. McMahon 3.2
# On the line with an X: the first s changes one "an" and prints; the second
# s finds the remaining "an" (replaced text is never rescanned) and prints
# again. The third s groups words with \( \) and the replacement reorders
# them by number, so "In XANadu did Kubla KhAN" comes out reshuffled.
# Try: add g to the first s and see why the second then prints nothing.
#ARGS -n
/X/s/an/AN/p
/X/s/an/AN/gp
/X/s/^\(.*\) \(.*\) \(.*\) \(.*\)$/\4 \3 \2 \1/p

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
